      "writtenOn": "2021-02-13T02:23:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Daniel, can you help make this new HAL set optional following the new patterns?  I\u0027d like to avoid the special-purpose device config they\u0027ve had to add and gain the annotation support.",
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8bfe6332_e55a97f7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-05T20:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In broad strokes:\nWe shouldn\u0027t have a separate unsol for initialized.  This isn\u0027t used for anything other than when you can ask for contacts, but the ask is already asynchronous, so we don\u0027t need the extra step.  Let me know what you think\n\nBreak out the contact-capacity into a separate request/response pair.\n\nThe use of unsol for the batch reads makes me sad.  I was going to push back on it but using the request response-message multiple times would just be a nightmare in the ril.java code.  I understand why you did what you did - very pragmatic.  I would like to fix that eventually, but it couldn\u0027t be done now.  \n\nTo mitigate the risk of the unsol, I think we need to have a request serial# that the unsols include.",
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "313650a1_e2dcdb6b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1606087
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-08T20:26:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is an optimization that is supported by just one vendor, I think it\u0027s best to tie this to it\u0027s own capability at the HAL level.\n\nI updated the HOW TO doc with directions on how to do this.  I also used this use case in the example.\n\nFYI, the change to prevent blocking when getting the capabilities is pending code review.",
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28a696a3_7f210000",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-05T20:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is an asynchronous call anyway.  Why do we need this extra step.\n\nCan\u0027t we just block and return the contents after the init is done?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 499,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6eb1e0c4_a29b15af",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1156349
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T10:22:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, telephony doesn’t get SIM phonebook at boot up, then the “initdone” isn\u0027t necessary during the whole process. But once a new requirement to query the record immediately after SIM ready, then it rather need this indication to ensure modem side is ready. Otherwise if modem is not ready, it will get failure immediately, or if blocking till ready, the wakelock from RILJ might time out.\n\nFurthermore, how about renaming the ”phonebookInitDone” to “SimPhoneBookReady” to exactly express this indication, just like existing SIM ready indication? Only after this explicit indication, the client could load SIM phonebook gracefully.",
      "parentUuid": "28a696a3_7f210000",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 499,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b85860e_aa52c84f",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 507,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-05T20:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we should include another int32_t token from the caller. This should be included in each of the unsol we get back so the caller can know these apply to their request.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 507,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 507,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e560aff0_40b601df",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadio.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 507,
      "author": {
        "id": 1156349
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T10:22:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently other async APIs like startNetworkScan don’t have the token, so we follow the same. And in qcril/QMI, no token are used either. \n\nIn case of multiple or duplicated requests on one sub, they will be queued and returned only once after completion, see mAdnLoadingWaiters in https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/opt/telephony/+/1440475/18/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/SimPhoneBookRecordCache.java#144.\n\nBesides, if adding the token, RIL could just store the token but almost does nothing. So can we keep the current design?",
      "parentUuid": "5b85860e_aa52c84f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 507,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 507,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50c64d6d_66cefc0c",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadioIndication.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 127,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-05T20:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I commented on the previous file.  I\u0027d rather not have this.  It\u0027s not gating anything else so it seems like it\u0027s just part of the work needed to read the contacts.  Lets just block that on the modem/ril side until it\u0027s ready.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 127,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
