        "uuid": "cacfc624_a5dcaedb",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadioIndication.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 127,
      "author": {
        "id": 1156349
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T10:22:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just as commented previously, to improve the flexibility, we\u0027d better keep it, and maybe we could rename the indication to simPhoneBookStatusChanged? Or simPhoneBookReady?",
      "parentUuid": "50c64d6d_66cefc0c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 127,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "151bb30d_4c749855",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadioIndication.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 139,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-05T20:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we shouldn\u0027t depend on doing this math.  We need a status included which can give error indications and a terminal indication.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 139,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "459b92a7_aa5a6168",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadioIndication.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 139,
      "author": {
        "id": 1156349
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-09T10:22:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SIM phonebook capacity would be 3000 SIM records at max (according to SIM type), and both QMI/HIDL message have the data transmission limitation, that’s why there will be multiple indications to pass the data. \n\nHowever, we couldn’t guarantee the QMI indication order in RIL, that’s why we do the calculation according to the capacity and received AND in telephony at the end. \n\nIf not doing math in telephony, RIL still need to do that eventually. If unsol indications couldn’t guarantee the order either, that will be the problem (correct me if I’m wrong).  \n\nBesides, considering that one more indication still need additional logics, could we keep current design?",
      "parentUuid": "151bb30d_4c749855",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 139,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "29bd6a45f5f46c53a5082e83035d9ffc9a0160c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a55a9ac_8aaae7b1",
        "filename": "radio/1.6/IRadioIndication.hal",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 142,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-05T20:08:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should have \nIndtype,\nint for the token from the request that started this sequence\npbReceivedStatus (error, continues, done)\nvec\u003cPRI\u003e records",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 142,
        "startChar": 36,
